---
import Navigation from "../components/Navigation.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import "@fontsource/work-sans";
import "@fontsource/work-sans/700.css";
import "../styles/global.css";
import "../styles/colophon.css";
import { Font } from "astro:assets";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta
      name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover"
    />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <link
      rel="icon"
      type="image/png"
      href="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81783950"
    />
    <Font cssVariable="--font-open-sauce-sans" preload />
    <Font cssVariable="--font-open-sans" preload />
    <Font cssVariable="--font-archivo-black" preload />
    <title>abucky.dev</title>
    <link rel="sitemap" href="/sitemap-index.xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Navigation currentPath={Astro.url.pathname} />
    <main class="main-content">
      <h1>Colophon</h1>
      <h2>01. About This Site</h2>
      <p>
        This website was built in the summer of 2025 as a random weekday project
        since I had nothing to do between graduating high school and starting
        college. It started as just a blog, homepage, and about me template
        website in Astro.<br /><br />

        The website has gone through three different design iterations. The
        first was a relatively basic white-on-black website. Because it was only
        my second full website, it was more focused on just making it unique
        than actually visually interesting. <br /><br />

        The second iteration went in a similar direction, but had a
        black-grey-black linear gradient with a grid on top, and a fade to
        darker black under the main content. I didn't end up finishing the
        implementation of this one because I started having issues with how to
        organize the homepage to where everything felt like it flowed properly.<br
        /><br />

        The third iteration went back to a similar idea to the first design, but
        with a more complimentary dark-gray background and very light-gray text.
        I kept the background as a solid color to make organization easier, and
        decided to keep the homepage simple without trying to fit a bunch of
        random stuff on it.
      </p>
      <h2>02. Built With</h2>
      <p>
        This website was built with Astro, React Components, and raw CSS. I
        don't remember the exact reason for choosing Astro, but if I recall
        correctly I googled best website frameworks or something similar and
        Astro kept being recommended. I <em>heavily</em> recommend Astro for personal
        sites, it's super easy to setup and use. Most of the website is static content,
        except for the now playing box on the homepage or the Guestbook (soon™).<br
        /><br />

        The website is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, and the backend apis are
        hosted on Cloudflare Functions (such as the Last.fm api wrapper or the
        (soon™ to be implemented) Guestbook).
      </p>
      <h2>03. Design</h2>
      <p>
        The current design of this website was built in Canva, and I
        experimented with different layouts before implementing what I designed
        in Astro and CSS. I settled on a Dark Gray (#424242) background and
        Light Gray (#d9d9d9) for text. All body text and headers use Open Sans,
        titles of pages use Archivo Black, and the logo uses Open Sauce Sans.
      </p>
      <h2>04. Credits</h2>
      <p>
        Fonts: Open Sans, Open Sauce, & Archivo Black <br />
        Icons: Font Awesome, SVG Repo, & Devicons.
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
